<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:03Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Swiss glaciers lose more than 5% in ice volume in 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2526affc1583fb699d7700ed5dd21c68638a7e0268d4756da4f05a73a2c75a9c</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T03:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/swiss-glaciers-lose-more-than-5-in-ice-volume-in-2026/a-79495965--ebd2291f40e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/swiss-glaciers-lose-more-than-5-in-ice-volume-in-2026/a-79495965?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the last five years, Swiss glaciers have lost nearly 20% of their mass, and 2026 saw the second-biggest loss of glacier volume on record. Experts warn there could be no ice left in the next 10-15 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US military cuts generals, admirals by 20%, Hegseth says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5aea675a20d508b04ba2346e1684a04fd34e76dcdfdff3d857895d0a036f547</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:10:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T01:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-military-cuts-generals-admirals-by-20-hegseth-says/a-79495683--79e31e8a192e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-military-cuts-generals-admirals-by-20-hegseth-says/a-79495683?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US defense secretary has also unveiled major changes, including a new drone command and an Elon Musk-led task force to assess the future of warfare.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested as student protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26c1f51b1e28c3ee8efe1e72a7ecbc8131e039eedecaefc0595366f8d1aa2286</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633--b363f8aabae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Student protests have grown in scale and intensity, with violent clashes in some places leading to hundreds of arrests and dozens of injuries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: NGO reports dire camp conditions, says Israel is moving 'Yellow Line'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b2dc517da4391888d73c4fc745f926d4864142010ef319e8732478476b7e297</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:11:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T22:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777--aae790bffc81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gaza-ngo-reports-dire-camp-conditions-says-israel-is-moving-yellow-line/a-79488777?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Danish Refugee Council alleges that Israel is employing "a policy of protracted displacement" in Gaza. It says the so-called "Yellow Line" is creeping west toward the coast, preventing many from returning home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f90e415f1dd81db3d3ff71acb0bea9b09d2bfba8538692928a6242c6e4ac096</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers outside the EU. An African partner country has reportedly already been selected.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Flydubai pilot investigated over possible attempt to crash Tel Aviv-bound flight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed522859fb4dbe428887eadb150e89b69fdc03236ca771dfc4660ca114da98a8</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flydubai-pilot-investigated-over-possible-attempt-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-flight/a-79484761--24ed602fb272.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flydubai-pilot-investigated-over-possible-attempt-to-crash-tel-aviv-bound-flight/a-79484761?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Flydubai service from the UAE to Israel made an emergency landing after the copilot stabbed the captain. Eyewitnesses said he attempted to crash the plane before he was subdued by passengers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's Macron, Spain's Sanchez welcome idea of UK rejoining EU after Burnham remarks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:737967385f0e30777e7277b76eeaa460f2d3c7438f827af4514a127e8e22c855</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-macron-spain-s-sanchez-welcome-idea-of-uk-rejoining-eu-after-burnham-remarks/a-79493469--0632af9b0576.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-macron-spain-s-sanchez-welcome-idea-of-uk-rejoining-eu-after-burnham-remarks/a-79493469?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During a visit to Spain, France's Emmanuel Macron said it would be "good news" if the UK moves towards the EU, with Pedro Sanchez also embracing the idea. UK PM Andy Burnham has not ruled out rejoining the bloc.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Are the Houthis winning against Saudi Arabia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:107f9549aaebbe3b447ced5dc477ffaf62465d837bdb296b59198ae4a0289e5e</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-the-houthis-winning-against-saudi-arabia/a-79492476--c9910a2a90c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-the-houthis-winning-against-saudi-arabia/a-79492476?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's unclear how the Saudis can defuse the threat presented by the Houthis in next-door Yemen or who they can turn to for help. The US isn't interested, the Europeans are hedging and nobody wants open conflict with Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany debates alleged antisemitism in the Left Party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e8866758b9398dc2b6dfd79cd5f611f6d5f3eab34b4b302bd61fef9e986a472</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T16:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-debates-alleged-antisemitism-in-the-left-party/a-79493282--492f53fcd817.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-debates-alleged-antisemitism-in-the-left-party/a-79493282?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Central Council of Jews in Germany thinks the Left Party is dangerous. Other Jews, however, are showing solidarity with the party. How does that add up?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's Youth Olympics makes Olympics in Africa 'logical'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94e4435ef3479f80f20d41dba1df59b19a7eb733a461fe2d4c997b3ceac7eb51</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975--7dbe2801c775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Youth Olympics are to be hosted in Africa for the first time ever. The edition in Senegal is also a chance to prove the continent can host a full Olympics in the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>African leaders herald $16B Dangote oil refinery in Kenya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0d5789a72ba837bfb17583d55649b448315b748743c42ca278bdc18508fbd5e</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T15:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/african-leaders-herald-16b-dangote-oil-refinery-in-kenya/a-79491068--44c455a72b9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/african-leaders-herald-16b-dangote-oil-refinery-in-kenya/a-79491068?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An oil refinery on Kenya's coast is expected to be completed in 40 months, and will process an estimated 700,000 barrels of oil per day. Africa's richest man, Aliko Dangote, will lead the project.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany raises Deutschlandticket price to €66.80 a month from 2027 under new cost-based formula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24e066fb4048ae4bc1df1664119a73a8535eaace0d073aba0da0cd961339cc6c</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-raises-deutschlandticket-price-to-_66-80-a-month-from-2027-under-new-cost-based-formula/a-79492524--e67f73547557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-raises-deutschlandticket-price-to-€66-80-a-month-from-2027-under-new-cost-based-formula/a-79492524?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new cost-based formula has pushed up the price of Germany's nationwide public transport pass for 2027.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's nuclear program remains shrouded in mystery as the regime debates ditching non-proliferation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8b94c4b7d81b236c722bcd6134d4c03227bb35e1f7ca0da675c3272fd033411</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197--eb083345c8e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-nuclear-program-remains-shrouded-in-mystery-as-the-regime-debates-ditching-non-proliferation/a-79488197?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's nuclear program is entering a critical phase as Tehran debates dropping out of a nuclear non-proliferation treaty. Satellite images also show activity at known nuclear sites.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d881def575a8c7ce88d1fe5aece770a4dd00a378339205fc83a556466fbb33da</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fullbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2b4be4694f34226de860e5298969eeceba03fafccb9eb0f4eb6d4155c944660</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City have become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c326782d6b8c9fa708dc4ca5f3f8cb44ffffb5bff3909f6bb61bca770f58e03</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff at the Wiesn are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism. They're taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia elections: Polls overshadowed by exhaustion, exodus and geopolitics as ethnic politics eclipse real problems</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a5e4898ffd7faf559425db90dddeca15301d57dff2635fc87111f93bf2006fe</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-/a-79487802--91e658c381f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-real-problems/a-79487802?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia goes to the polls on October 4 to elect several parliaments and presidents. While voters worry about the economy and emigration, the campaign is focused on ethnicity, exposing the country's political paralysis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is US President Donald Trump right to rename AI as 'Super Intelligence'?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e4eb2420993afcf71f4621e0216bd03b1924b0890d4fc0cb202ed4a3bf40e01</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388--e5323453fe90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-us-president-donald-trump-right-to-rename-ai-as-super-intelligence/a-79430388?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump thinks the name artificial intelligence sounds "fake" and has ordered US agencies to use "Super Intelligence" instead. Yet, tech firms and researchers have little reason to play along.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a36e45aba9eab808c68f3de0346f9215c1ed8ae319e8b6451923da0711ca629f</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea: Lost shark draws over half a million visitors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b91d57a894922ac32a663cd9155232174b34becfd108fc5b5a40996941e1bee5</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014--618815d2f667.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-lost-shark-draws-over-half-a-million-visitors/a-79482014?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The South Korean port of Busan says that a stranded shark has become a major tourist draw. It's also named the ocean predator an honorary ambassador to the city.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Eiffel Tower chief Patrick Branco Ruivo to step down after female staff excluded during Hindu group's visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e5a6be1e8d9efc9cdb7d6dd30764cca658a30cbf8739f8c0781a4f3e2818550</id><updated>2026-10-01T06:09:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T08:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eiffel-tower-chief-patrick-branco-ruivo-to-step-down-after-female-staff-excluded-during-hindu-group-/a-79482406--4df26f6b2ddb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eiffel-tower-chief-patrick-branco-ruivo-to-step-down-after-female-staff-excluded-during-hindu-group-s-visit/a-79482406?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An investigation found management failures led to female Eiffel Tower staff being excluded during a Hindu group's visit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
